==== ex01 ====
ft_range
Turn-in directory: ex01/
Files to turn in: ft_range.c
Allowed functions: malloc
• Create a function ft_range which returns an array of ints. This int array should
contain all values between min and max.
• Min included - max excluded.
• Here is how it should be prototyped :
int *ft_range(int min, int max);
• If the value of min is greater than or equal to max, a NULL pointer should be
returned.
**************

char string
→ 通常需要 '\0'
→ malloc(len + 1)

int array
→ 没有 '\0'
→ malloc(number_of_ints)

#include <stdlib.h>

int	*ft_range(int min, int max)
{
	int	*range;
	int	size;
	int	i;

	if (min >= max)
		return (0);
	size = max - min;
	range = malloc(sizeof(int) * size);
	if (!range)
		return (0);
	i = 0;
	while (i < size)
	{
		range[i] = min + i;
		i++;
	}
	return (range);
}
